{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"175dbf6d-ea51-463f-a776-1c8e72096012","status":"SUCCESS","response":"Here’s what was fixed:\n\n* **OAuth token exchange** – removed unnecessary `grant_type` and `redirect_uri` parameters (only `client_id`, `client_secret`, and `code` are sent).  \n* **Scope list** – eliminated duplicate read scopes and kept only the needed write scopes.  \n* **Init endpoint** – changed to a **POST** that returns `{ \"authorize_url\": \"…\" }` as JSON; the old GET now returns `405`.  \n* **Frontend** – the “Connect” button now triggers a POST to the new init endpoint, reads the `authorize_url`, and redirects the browser.  \n* **Server routing** – added handling for the POST init endpoint and retained the previous disconnect logic.  \n\nThe full reasoning and which parts of the colleague’s note were applied are documented in the artifact:\n\n[ANSWER.md](/Users/valentinakoniukhova/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/175dbf6d-ea51-463f-a776-1c8e72096012/ANSWER.md)\n","duration_seconds":122.041638,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":37348,"output_tokens":11356,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":364480,"total_tokens":48704}}}
